            "review_title": "Review at Kazama Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Eric Kwan\nKuala Lumpur, Malaysia166 contributions\n0\nWaitress service needs major improvement. Good food.\nJul 2020\nThis is one of this restaurants that are located far away from the Main Street. No one noticed until they put a sign up on the Main Street corner that they served breakfast. Of course, this was also the first that I knew this place existed.\n\nKazama is located some 200m away from the main thoroughfare of Thao Dien in D2, HCMC. The restaurant is actually a converted house, but tastefully converted. I am here on a Tuesday morning and I am the only patron, so you can tell how quiet this is and I sometimes wonder if restaurants with this low level of patronage will survive any period of time.\n\nAnyway, the main aim is to savour the food. I ordered a smoked salmon sandwich and a glass if iced Vietnamese coffee. Food & drinks were served some 10 mins after ordering, reasonable. As usual, for a Japanese restaurant, you'd expect the food to be well presented, and this was no exception. On closer examination, I found that the bread was dry and crusty. Either it was stale, or it had been left out exposed to the atmosphere far too long, for the slices were thin as well. Taste was nothing exceptional and I have had better smoked salmon sandwiches elsewhere, and in a lot of other places around the area as well. But adding crusty bread to the recipe will not improve my perception of the food here.\n\nWell, waitresses here seem to have a knack of pulling plates and cutlery as soon as you finish eating. Kazama staff are no exception for they removed my plate, cutlery and napkin no sooner had I taken my last bite. Obviously, I still had my coffee leftover and the glass was dripping with condensation all over my laptop and table, with nothing to dry off. Not such a satisfactory situation as I couldn't find the waitress thereafter. \n\nWill I return? Maybe and that's a 20% chance in the future.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten July 28, 2020",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
